{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Doctor, Mrs. Menon is in. Her daughter is on the bench outside, she refused to let her come in.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. What brings you?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): Nothing brings me. I am tired and she dragged me. I slid down, she panicked, that is the whole story.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): How many times did you go down?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): Twice. It was not a fall. The legs went soft and I slid.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): The daughter told me outside it was four times in this fortnight, and one night she was on the bathroom floor and could not get up for some time.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): Nonsense. Twice only. I was not lying there stuck. She makes a mountain of it.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): When were those two?",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): First was Sunday... no, Monday, getting off the cot. Second was day before yesterday, by the washbasin.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): Giddy beforehand?",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): Yes. I get up and the room turns a little, then I go down.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Is it every time you stand?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): Not every time. Mostly mornings, and if I get up fast from the chair.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): Did you black out?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): No. I was awake the whole time. I could hear the cooker, so I know.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Hit your head at all?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Daughter said the left elbow got bruised that bathroom night.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): That mark is from the cupboard last month. Old. I did not bump anything this time, I am tired of saying it.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Chest pain when the giddiness comes?",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): Breathless?",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (PATIENT): No. I feel washed out, that is all, and I am seventy-eight, what else.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): Palpitations?",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (PATIENT): Sometimes at night the heart runs. Not with the sliding.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): How many weeks for the giddiness?",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (PATIENT): Two weeks... actually three weeks. Worse after they increased a BP tablet.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Which tablet, what dose now?",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (PATIENT): Amlodipine ten milligrams in the morning after tea. Earlier it was five, they put it up.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): Who did that, and when?",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (PATIENT): Clinic doctor near the market, about a month back. Said the pressure was not controlled.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Other BP medicines?",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (PATIENT): Telmisartan forty... no, eighty milligrams, after dinner. And atenolol fifty milligrams in the morning with the amlodipine.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): And for sleep?",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (PATIENT): Zolpidem. I nearly said ten milligrams, but the strip is five. Five milligrams when I lie down.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (PATIENT): Don't mix it up with my sister's bottle. She keeps metformin in my drawer when she stays, for her diabetes. I have never taken that.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): Do you miss doses of your own?",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (PATIENT): I don't. Both morning ones after tea, telmisartan after dinner, zolpidem at bedtime.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke, or take alcohol?",
  "[SEG0040] person_3 (PATIENT): Never smoked. No alcohol. Tea, yes, three cups, sometimes four.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (DOCTOR): Living alone?",
  "[SEG0042] person_3 (PATIENT): Alone, yes. Daughter is two streets away. Maid comes one hour in the morning. She was late yesterday, milk boiled over, kitchen was a sight, but leave that.",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (DOCTOR): Nurse, lying and standing readings.",
  "[SEG0044] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Lying, one forty-six over eighty-four... sorry, one forty-eight over eighty-six, pulse sixty-eight. Standing after three minutes, I said one eighteen over seventy-four by mistake, correct figure is one twelve over seventy, pulse eighty-eight. She was giddy while standing and held the couch.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (DOCTOR): Clear drop. Let me look.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (DOCTOR): Heart sounds are normal, no murmur. Chest is clear.",
  "[SEG0047] person_2 (DOCTOR): No one-sided weakness. Hands have no tremor.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (DOCTOR): On the left elbow I see only a faint old mark, nothing fresh.",
  "[SEG0049] person_2 (DOCTOR): Stand for a moment. You sway once you are upright. Sit back down.",
  "[SEG0050] person_3 (PATIENT): You have seen it now. Can we finish, I want my own cot, not this chair.",
  "[SEG0051] person_2 (DOCTOR): This is a postural drop from the pressure tablets, mainly since amlodipine became ten. I am not thinking of a stroke.",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (DOCTOR): Because you say the room spins, I cannot fully rule out an inner-ear cause, but the standing pressure comes first.",
  "[SEG0053] person_2 (DOCTOR): I am changing one tablet. From tomorrow amlodipine is five milligrams in the morning. Keep telmisartan eighty, atenolol fifty, and zolpidem five as they are.",
  "[SEG0054] person_3 (PATIENT): That other doctor will say I spoiled the control. He increased it only last month.",
  "[SEG0055] person_2 (DOCTOR): We will watch the readings. Sit at the edge of the cot before you stand. If you black out or go down again, come the same day.",
  "[SEG0056] person_2 (DOCTOR): ECG today, and blood for sodium and kidney function. Come back in two weeks, and bring the home pressure readings your daughter takes.",
  "[SEG0057] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): I will take her across for the ECG. Walk with me slowly, blood room is still open."
 ],
